16.8 Two Objects Example

Counter c1 = new Counter();
Counter c2 = new Counter();

Thread-A
c1.increment();

Thread-B
c2.increment();

Question

Can both execute simultaneously?
✅ Yes.
Because

Monitor(c1) ≠ Monitor(c2)

Different objects.
Different monitors.


16.9 Summary (Interview Revision)
🔴 A synchronized instance method acquires the monitor of the current object (this).
🔴 Only one thread can execute synchronized instance methods guarded by the same object at a time.
🔴 Other threads attempting to enter synchronized methods on that object enter the BLOCKED state.
🔴 Different object instances have different monitors, so synchronization is independent across instances.
🔴 Synchronized methods are a simple way to protect shared mutable state from race conditions.